/**
 * The past-records import guide, copied from talimBE-V2 `docs/history-import-guide.md`
 * by `npm run guide:import`. Do not edit it here: change the backend's guide and run
 * the script again.
 */
export const HISTORY_IMPORT_GUIDE = "# Importing your past records into Talim\n\nThis guide is for school admins (and bursars or records officers helping them). It explains how to\nbring your school's past years into Talim: sessions, classes, subjects, teachers, students, and every\nscore and report-card detail. Once imported, former students can sign in and see their results and\ntranscript, and your staff can see each student's full history.\n\nYou fill in one Excel workbook (the **template**), upload it, check the report Talim gives you, and\nconfirm. Nothing is saved until you confirm.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Before you start\n\nHave these to hand for every session (school year) you want to import:\n\n- the session dates, and the dates of each term that has **already ended**;\n- your class list (classes are permanent: \"JSS 1A\" is the same class every year);\n- your subjects and short codes (for example `MTH` for Mathematics);\n- the teachers who taught in those years, including those who have left;\n- every student who attended: current students, graduates, and those who left;\n- which class each student was in each session, and how the session ended for them;\n- the scores for every assessment (for example CA 1, CA 2, Exam);\n- optionally: attendance totals, class teacher's and principal's remarks, and positions.\n\nDownload the template in School Admin: **Settings → Data → Import past records → Download template**.\n\n## 2. The workbook\n\nThe template has:\n\n- **Instructions**: a summary of this guide and a list of every column.\n- **One sheet per kind of record** (Sessions, Terms, Classes, ...). Each starts empty with its\n  header row. Yellow headers are required; grey ones are optional. Hover over a header to see what\n  goes in it.\n- **Examples**: filled-in sample rows for every sheet. Talim ignores this sheet when you upload, so\n  you can leave it in the file. Do not copy its rows into the other sheets unless they are really\n  your data.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Keep the sheet names and the header row. Columns can be in any order; extra columns are ignored.\n- Dates are written `YYYY-MM-DD`, for example `2021-09-13`. Dates typed as Excel dates also work.\n- Write names the same way on every sheet. Capital letters and extra spaces do not matter\n  (`JSS 1A`, `jss 1a` and `JSS  1A` are the same class), but spelling does (`JSS1A` is different).\n- One file can hold up to 1,000,000 scores and be at most 50 MB. A bigger school can split its\n  history into several files (for example one per session); import them one after the other.\n- Instead of a workbook you can upload a ZIP of CSV files named after the sheets (`Sessions.csv`,\n  `Terms.csv` ...), saved as UTF-8.\n\n## 3. The sheets, column by column\n\n`*` marks a required column.\n\n### Sessions\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `session`* | `2021/2022` | Other sheets refer to the session by this name. |\n| `start_date`* | `2021-09-13` | |\n| `end_date`* | `2022-07-22` | |\n\nSessions must not overlap each other or a session already in Talim. A session that is already in\nTalim (same name) is matched and its dates are kept.\n\n### Terms\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `session`* | `2021/2022` | As in Sessions. |\n| `term`* | `First Term` | Unique within its session. |\n| `start_date`* | `2021-09-13` | Inside the session's dates. |\n| `end_date`* | `2021-12-17` | Must be before today: only finished terms can be imported. |\n| `days_open` | `62` | Days the school opened. Blank: Talim counts the school days between the dates (your school days, less holidays). |\n\n### Classes\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `class`* | `JSS 1A`, `SS 2 Science` | A class already in Talim is matched by name. |\n| `level`* | `JSS 1` ... `SS 3` | The year group. Use `JSS 1` to `SS 3` if you can; your own labels also work. |\n| `level_order`* | `1` | 1 for the first year, 2 for the next... The highest number is the graduating level. |\n| `stream` | `Science` | Optional. |\n\n### Subjects\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `subject_code`* | `MTH` | Short code used on the other sheets. |\n| `subject`* | `Mathematics` | |\n\nTalim stores the code with your school's prefix (`MTH` becomes `CVC-MTH`) because subject codes are\nunique across Talim. You always write the short code; re-imports find the same subject.\n\n### Teachers\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `staff_number` | `T014` | A staff number **or** an email is required. |\n| `first_name`* | `Amaka` | |\n| `last_name`* | `Okafor` | |\n| `email` | `amaka.okafor@school.ng` | Without one, the account is kept inactive. |\n| `phone` | `08031234567` | |\n| `gender` | `female` | `male` or `female`. |\n| `still_at_school` | `yes` | `yes` or `no` (default `yes`). A teacher who left gets an inactive account. |\n\nTeachers already in Talim are matched by staff number or email and are not changed.\n\n### ClassSubjects\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `class`* | `JSS 1A` | As in Classes. |\n| `subject_code`* | `MTH` | As in Subjects. |\n| `teacher` | `T014` or `amaka.okafor@school.ng` | The subject teacher, by staff number or email. |\n\nOne row per subject a class takes. A subject a class already has in Talim keeps its current teacher.\n\n### Students\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `admission_number`* | `CVC/2020/0143` | Unique in your school. |\n| `first_name`* | `Tolu` | |\n| `last_name`* | `Adebayo` | |\n| `other_names` | `Grace` | Middle names (shown after the first name). |\n| `gender` | `female` | |\n| `date_of_birth` | `2008-04-12` | |\n| `email` | `tolu@example.com` | The student's own email. Without one the student cannot sign in until you add it. |\n| `parent_name` | `Funke Adebayo` | |\n| `parent_phone` | `08021234567` | |\n| `parent_email` | `funke@example.com` | A parent already on Talim (even at another school) is linked, not created again. |\n| `parent_relationship` | `MOTHER` | `MOTHER`, `FATHER`, `GUARDIAN` or `OTHER` (default `GUARDIAN`). |\n| `status`* | `graduated` | `active`, `graduated`, `withdrawn`, `transferred` or `left`. |\n| `left_session` | `2023/2024` | The session they graduated or left in. Blank: the session of their last enrollment. |\n| `transfer_school` | `royal-heritage-ibadan` | For `transferred` only: the Talim school they moved to (its Talim code, which that school can give you). Required for `transferred`. |\n| `transfer_admission_number` | `RHS/2024/0007` | For `transferred`: their admission number at that school, so the two records can be joined. |\n\n- `transferred` means the student moved to **another school on Talim**. Their record at both schools\n  becomes one record, and their transcript shows both schools. It does not matter which school\n  imports first. For a move to a school that is not on Talim, use `left`.\n- Students without a parent email get a parent contact that cannot sign in until you add an email.\n\n### Enrollments\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `admission_number`* | `CVC/2020/0143` | As in Students. |\n| `session`* | `2021/2022` | |\n| `class`* | `JSS 2A` | |\n| `outcome`* | `promoted` | `promoted`, `repeated`, `graduated`, `withdrawn`, `transferred`, or `continuing`. |\n\nOne row per student per session they attended (never two classes in one session). The outcome must\nagree with the student's status:\n\n| Status | Last enrollment's outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| `active` | `continuing`, `promoted` or `repeated` |\n| `graduated` | `graduated` (only from a class at the top `level_order`) |\n| `withdrawn` | `withdrawn` |\n| `transferred` | `transferred` |\n| `left` | `promoted`, `repeated` or `withdrawn` |\n\n`graduated`, `withdrawn`, `transferred` and `continuing` can only be on a student's last enrollment.\n`continuing` is only for the session that is running now. Set the current session up in Talim first\n(the session and its current term), and the import will find it.\n\n### Assessments\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `session`* | `2021/2022` | |\n| `term`* | `First Term` | |\n| `assessment`* | `CA 1` | |\n| `max_score`* | `20` | A whole number from 1 to 1000. |\n| `order` | `1` | Its place on the report card. Blank: the order of the rows. |\n\nThe same assessments apply to every class that term.\n\n### Scores\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `admission_number`* | `CVC/2020/0143` | |\n| `session`* | `2021/2022` | |\n| `term`* | `First Term` | |\n| `subject_code`* | `MTH` | The student's class (from Enrollments) must take this subject (ClassSubjects). |\n| `assessment`* | `CA 1` | As in Assessments for that term. |\n| `score`* | `17.5` | From 0 to the max score, at most 2 decimals. Leave it blank if there was no score: the subject then shows as incomplete. |\n| `teacher` | `T014` | Who recorded it. Blank: the subject teacher. |\n\nOne row per student, term, subject and assessment. Talim works out the totals, percentages, grades\n(on your grading scale) and positions exactly as it does for live results.\n\n### TermResults\n\n| Column | Example | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `admission_number`* | `CVC/2020/0143` | |\n| `session`* | `2021/2022` | |\n| `term`* | `First Term` | |\n| `days_present` | `59` | If you give only present or only absent, the other is the days open less it. |\n| `days_absent` | `3` | Present plus absent cannot be more than the days the school opened. |\n| `class_teacher_remark` | `A hardworking student.` | Up to 500 characters. |\n| `principal_remark` | `Keep it up.` | Up to 500 characters. |\n| `position` | `3` | Blank: Talim works the position out from the scores. Fill it in only to keep your own. |\n\nThis sheet is optional; a student with scores gets a report card without it.\n\n## 4. Uploading and checking\n\n1. **Upload** the file. Talim checks every row of every sheet against the rest of the file and\n   against what is already in Talim. This takes a few seconds to a minute.\n2. **Read the report.**\n   - **Errors** must be fixed. Each one gives the sheet, the row, the column and what to do. Download\n     the full list as a CSV (*Download errors*) and work through it in Excel.\n   - **Warnings** do not stop the import, but read them (for example: a teacher without an email, a\n     class whose level differs from the one in Talim, a transfer school not yet on Talim).\n   - The counts show how many rows of each sheet were read.\n3. Fix the file and upload it again until there are no errors.\n4. **Confirm** the import. Talim writes everything in the background and shows its progress. A\n   school of 600 students and 140,000 scores takes under a minute.\n\nNobody is notified or emailed by an import.\n\n## 5. After the import\n\n- Past sessions and terms are closed. Results are published as of each term's end, so students and\n  parents see them on report cards.\n- Graduates and leavers keep their login, read-only: they see their results and transcript.\n- **Signing in.** Imported accounts get no password and no email. Each person signs in with\n  *Forgot password* on their email, or you reset their password from their profile. They are asked\n  to choose a new password the first time.\n- People imported without an email have an address ending in `.import.mytalim.test` and are kept\n  inactive. Edit their email in Talim (and activate the account) when you have it.\n\n## 6. Importing again\n\nYou can import the same file again (for example after correcting scores). Talim matches everything\nby its name, code or admission number:\n\n- rows from an earlier import are updated, and those you removed from the file are removed from Talim;\n- nothing is created twice;\n- records entered directly in Talim are never changed. A term that already has results entered in\n  Talim cannot receive imported results (remove that term's assessments, scores and term results from\n  the file);\n- students and teachers who were already in Talim keep their profile as it is; only their past\n  records are added.\n\nIf an import stops with an error while writing, open it and confirm it again: it picks up safely\nwhere it stopped.\n\n## 7. Common errors and how to fix them\n\n| Message (shortened) | What to do |\n| --- | --- |\n| *The column \"x\" is missing from the header row.* | Put the header back exactly as in the template. |\n| *Session \"x\" is not in Sessions or in Talim.* | Add the session to Sessions, or fix the spelling. The same goes for terms, classes, subjects, teachers and students. |\n| *Use a date like 2021-09-13.* | Write the date as `YYYY-MM-DD`. |\n| *\"Third Term\" has not ended.* | Only finished terms can be imported. Leave out the term in progress. |\n| *Session \"x\" overlaps session \"y\".* | Check both sessions' dates. |\n| *21 is more than CA 1's maximum of 20.* | Correct the score, or the assessment's `max_score`. |\n| *Use a number with at most 2 decimals.* | Round the score to 2 decimals. |\n| *MTH is not a subject of JSS 2A.* | Add the class and subject to ClassSubjects, or check the student's class in Enrollments. |\n| *Student \"x\" has no enrollment in 2021/2022, so their class is unknown.* | Add the student's class for that session to Enrollments. |\n| *Student \"x\" already has an enrollment in 2021/2022.* | Keep one class per student per session. |\n| *Status \"graduated\" does not match the last enrollment's outcome.* | Make the student's status and their last enrollment's outcome agree (see the table above). |\n| *Only the top level can graduate.* | Check `level_order` in Classes, or the student's last class. |\n| *continuing is only for the current session.* | Use `promoted` or `repeated` for a past session. Set the current session up in Talim first. |\n| *x@y.com already belongs to another Talim account.* | Use the person's own email, or leave it blank. |\n| *... belongs to a Talim account that is not a parent's.* | The parent email is a teacher's or a student's. Use the parent's own email. |\n| *... is already used for a teacher in this pack.* | Two people cannot share one email (siblings can share a parent's). |\n| *... already has results entered in Talim.* | Remove that term's rows from Assessments, Scores and TermResults. |\n| *A pack may hold at most 1,000,000 score rows.* | Split the file, for example one per session. |\n";
